Institutional Homeostasis
The capacity of an institution to preserve operational integrity, procedural consistency, accountability, and organizational stability while responding to internal deficiencies and external pressures.

Autonomic Institutional Homeostasis

A proposed framework in which an institution independently monitors, identifies, and corrects operational deviations through established feedback, oversight, and accountability mechanisms.






