 Institutional / technical application
Autonomic Institutional Integrity:

A conceptual framework in which institutional systems independently monitor, regulate, evaluate, and maintain their own operational integrity through established rules, controls, and accountability mechanisms.

Example: 
"The integrity protocol operates autonomically, identifying procedural deviations and initiating predefined corrective mechanisms without requiring continuous external direction."

Terminological note:
Autonomic is the more established adjective in technical English, particularly in autonomic computing and biological regulation. Autonomically is its adverb.


The central concept is self-regulation through continuous adjustment.






